<title>MEXICO: Banco de Mexico completes secondary participation.</title>
<headline>Banco de Mexico completes secondary participation.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco de Mexico assigned all three direct sales of paper and three repurchase agreements whereby it had sought to drain 1.975 billion pesos from the secondary market on Monday, dealers said.</p>
<p>The Cetes sales were placed as follows:</p>
<p>    AMOUNT     TERM	 AVERAGE RATE</p>
<p>    150 million    339 days   22.96 pct</p>
<p>    150 million    178 days   21.92 pct</p>
<p>    150 million     87 days   21.19 pct</p>
<p>The terms and maturities of the repurchase agreements were assigned as follows:</p>
<p>    670 million     25 days   19.09 pct</p>
<p>    670 million     18 days   18.92 pct</p>
<p>    185 million	1 day    17.89 pct</p>
<p>*Amounts in pesos</p>
<p>(( --Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9559))</p>
</text>
